      <description><![CDATA[<style>body{font:13px -apple-system,system-ui;line-height:1.45;color:#1d1d1f}h4{font-size:12px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.04em;color:#6e6e73;margin:14px 0 4px}ul{padding-left:18px;margin:0}li{margin:4px 0}code{font:12px ui-monospace,monospace}@media (prefers-color-scheme:dark){body{color:#f5f5f7}h4{color:#a1a1a6}}</style><h4>Highlights</h4>
<ul>
<li><strong>A set is one canvas.</strong> Drag a device onto the gap between two screens and it&#39;s pulled to sit exactly across both: the seam lights up and says &quot;Across 2 &amp; 3&quot;, either way along the set. Drag it mostly onto the screen beside it and it moves there. No settings needed (hold ⌥ to place it freely); a device&#39;s <strong>More options › Keep inside this screen</strong> cuts it off at its own screen&#39;s edges instead.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
